{
  "summary": "This experiment tested whether multiprofile avgpool aggregation could recover meaningful signal from the image modality, directly paralleling the RNA multiprofile experiment (llm_summary_004). Validation accuracy of ~32.8% (F1 ~28.8%) represents a ~12-point improvement over the image-only single-profile baseline (~20.8%, llm_summary_002), confirming that the single-profile limitation was a contributing factor to the image modality's apparent weakness, yet the image modality remains substantially weaker than the RNA-only multiprofile baseline (~65.0%). This suggests the image modality carries considerably less independent predictive signal than RNA even after multiprofile aggregation, though it remains uncertain whether alternative image encoders, more complex aggregation, or multimodal fusion could extract additional value from the residual image signal, and whether ~32.8% is near the practical ceiling for image-only multiprofile models."
}

